18. BeanPostProcessor

Very important senior interview topic.

It allows Spring to intercept beans before and after initialization.

java
@Component
public class MyBeanPostProcessor
        implements BeanPostProcessor {

    @Override
    public Object postProcessBeforeInitialization(
            Object bean,
            String beanName) {

        System.out.println("Before: " + beanName);

        return bean;
    }

    @Override
    public Object postProcessAfterInitialization(
            Object bean,
            String beanName) {

        System.out.println("After: " + beanName);

        return bean;
    }
}

Spring itself heavily relies on BeanPostProcessor.

For example, things involving:

@Autowired
@PostConstruct
AOP
@Transactional
@Async

involve sophisticated post-processing mechanisms.

