45. Spring Interview Questions You Should Know

Beginner → Intermediate

Q1. What is Spring?

Spring is a Java framework providing IoC, DI, AOP, transaction management, web development, data access and other infrastructure capabilities.

Q2. What is IoC?

Inversion of Control means object creation and dependency management are delegated to the Spring container.

Q3. What is DI?

Dependency Injection is the mechanism through which Spring provides required dependencies to objects.

Q4. What is a Spring Bean?

An object instantiated, configured, and managed by the Spring IoC container.

Q5. What is ApplicationContext?

An advanced Spring IoC container that provides bean management plus events, resources, i18n and other enterprise capabilities.

Q6. What is BeanFactory?

The fundamental Spring IoC container interface.

Q7. What are bean scopes?

singleton
prototype
request
session
application
websocket

Q8. What is the default scope?

singleton.

Q9. Singleton vs prototype?

One instance per container vs new instance per retrieval.

Q10. What is constructor injection?

Dependencies are supplied through the constructor.

46. Intermediate Spring Questions

Q11. @Component vs @Bean?

@Component is discovered by component scanning; @Bean explicitly registers an object returned by a configuration method.

Q12. @Service vs @Repository?

Both are component stereotypes, but @Service represents business logic while @Repository represents persistence logic and participates in exception translation.

Q13. What is @Primary?

Specifies the preferred bean when multiple candidates exist.

Q14. What is @Qualifier?

Explicitly identifies which bean should be injected.

Q15. What is @Lazy?

Delays bean initialization until the bean is required.

Q16. What is BeanPostProcessor?

An extension point allowing processing of beans before and after initialization.

Q17. What is BeanFactoryPostProcessor?

Processes bean-definition metadata before beans are instantiated.

Q18. What is circular dependency?

A → B
B → A

Constructor injection generally makes such cycles fail fast rather than allowing them to be hidden.

Q19. What is Spring AOP?

A mechanism for implementing cross-cutting concerns around method execution.

Q20. What is a Spring proxy?

An object wrapping the target bean and intercepting method calls to apply behavior such as transactions, caching or security.

